@* What the Web UI shows in place of every screen when sign-in is not
   configured (ADR 0245): the server runs with OIDC and has no client for the
   Web UI, or the settings name no mode the Web UI knows. It reads nothing
   from the server, and never behaves as anonymous. *@
<PageTitle>Sign-in is not configured · Varve</PageTitle>
<ViewHead Title="Sign-in is not configured" />
<Notice Title="This server has no sign-in for the Web UI" Warn="true">@if (Missing.Count > 0)
{<text>The server checks tokens from an issuer, and the Web UI has no client to ask it for one. Add </text>@for (int i = 0; i < Missing.Count; i++)
{@(i == 0 ? "" : i == Missing.Count - 1 ? " and " : ", ")<code>@Missing[i]</code>}<text> to the server's configuration, and restart it.</text>}
else
{<text>The Web UI's settings name no sign-in mode it knows: </text><code>Varve:Auth:Mode</code><text> is </text><code>Oidc</code><text> or </text><code>Anonymous</code><text>.</text>}</Notice>

@code {
    /// <summary>The settings the server names as missing; empty when the mode itself is missing or unknown.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Missing { get; set; } = [];
}
